Sections "STUDY" contain missmatched items: {'STUDY_SUMMARY': ["This study applies a nucleotidomics workflow that measures the metabolome and nucleotidome from the same extract by splitting each sample into paired aliquots — one treated with a nucleoside digestion mix (NEB M0649), one left native. Peak areas of the native aliquot are subtracted from the digested for each compound, allowing inference of the summed abundance of its phosphorylated derivatives whose phosphate groups are accessible to the digestion enzymes (∑P). Two pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) cell lines, Suit2-028 and Suit2-007, were profiled under control and gemcitabine (dFdC)-treated conditions (1 μM, 4 hours) by reversed-phase LC-MS with untargeted acquisition. The goals of this study were: (i) recapture of established gemcitabine mechanisms; (ii) untargeted analysis of gemcitabine's influence on the cellular metabolome and nucleotidome; (iii) exploration of expected and unexpected intracellular phosphate-bearing species (∑P). Three gemcitabine mechanisms of action were successfully recaptured: extensive phosphorylation of dFdC, ribonucleotide reductase inhibition, and the dFdU/thymidylate synthase axis. Untargeted analysis revealed deoxyinosine depletion, linked to reduced deoxyadenosine pools. Canonical (deoxy)nucleotides and (deoxy)nucleosides were captured within the dataset, along with several uncommon and unexpected nucleotide derivatives. The dataset is split into positive and negative polarities, both containing digested and native aliquots, iterative MS2 injections, QC samples, and blank extraction samples.", "This study applies a nucleotidomics workflow that measures the metabolome and nucleotidome from the same extract by splitting each sample into paired aliquots — one treated with a nucleoside digestion mix (NEB M0649), one left native. Peak areas of the native aliquot are subtracted from the digested for each compound, allowing inference of the summed abundance of its phosphorylated derivatives whose phosphate groups are accessible to the digestion enzymes (∑P). Two pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) cell lines, Suit2-028 and Suit2-007, were profiled under control and gemcitabine (dFdC)-treated conditions (1 μM, 4 hours) by reversed-phase LC-MS with untargeted acquisition. The goals of this study were: (i) recapture of established gemcitabine mechanisms; (ii) untargeted analysis of gemcitabine''s influence on the cellular metabolome and nucleotidome; (iii) exploration of expected and unexpected intracellular phosphate-bearing species (∑P). Three gemcitabine mechanisms of action were successfully recaptured: extensive phosphorylation of dFdC, ribonucleotide reductase inhibition, and the dFdU/thymidylate synthase axis. Untargeted analysis revealed deoxyinosine depletion, linked to reduced deoxyadenosine pools. Canonical (deoxy)nucleotides and (deoxy)nucleosides were captured within the dataset, along with several uncommon and unexpected nucleotide derivatives. The dataset is split into positive and negative polarities, both containing digested and native aliquots, iterative MS2 injections, QC samples, and blank extraction samples."]}